# L'Homme Luxe — Osmanthus Suede — Apricot Shadow — DHP 2025 V1

## Authority and status

Date 2026-09-02. 30 mL at 20% EdP: 6,000 uL concentrate + 24.00 mL ethanol. Source is immutable L'Homme Target-Native V5, Git-normalized SHA-256 `3709F1DB9E187B3C67215C3AA39B5D96DAC76B7B857631D7A020047D6C56F33E`. Status: `DESIGN HYPOTHESIS / COMPUTATIONAL / NOT TESTED / HOLD`. `NO COMPOUNDING / NO PROCUREMENT / NO SAFETY OR STABILITY CLEARANCE / NO PERFORMANCE CLAIM / NO RELEASE`.



## Target identity

Osmanthus is built as connected apricot skin, floral interior, violet cloth, fine suede and warm skin residue—not merely represented by one ingredient. The pleasure hypothesis is soft apricot light moving across tactile suede and polished mineral wood. Ginger gives a bright collection-recognition edge. Reject/HOLD for jam, peach candy, cosmetic iris, aggressive leather, rose clutter, tobacco, unrelated-natural muddiness, or powder takeover.

## Functional architecture before dosing

Ten target-native modules: restrained citrus air; bright ginger edge; apricot skin; osmanthus floral interior; violet cloth; fine suede fold; mineral cedar grain; warm sandal skin; slow fruit-suede matrix; sole Ambrettolide residue. Planes are front ginger/fruit skin, living osmanthus, folded violet suede, rear mineral wood, intimate wine-warm skin. Pressure is green fruit skin, ginger and mineral grain; release is floral tissue, Sandalore/Ebanol and the slow matrix.

