## Spatial, temporal, textural, transition, pressure/release, and recurrence maps

| Window | Intended transition | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| opening, 0-5 min | petitgrain/ginger exposes apricot skin | NOT TESTED |
| top, 5-30 min | apricot skin opens into osmanthus floral tissue | NOT TESTED |
| heart, 30-120 min | ionone cloth folds around restrained suede | NOT TESTED |
| late heart, 2-6 h | suede dries into mineral cedar and sandal skin | NOT TESTED |
| drydown, 6-24 h | tonka grain and Ambrettolide recall fruit warmth | NOT TESTED |

Ten links: citrus→ginger; ginger→apricot; damascone→osmanthus; osmanthus→ionone; ionone→suede; suede→Vetival; Vetival→cedar; cedar→sandal; sandal→tonka; tonka→Ambrettolide. Nineteen textures: bright; green; cut; apricot-skin; pulpy; petal; luminous; violet-cloth; fine-suede; dry; mineral; pencil-grain; rooty; polished; yielding; wine-warm; intimate; slow; skin-like. Recurrence is chemical: osmanthus ionone/damascone facets return through violet and the fruity-wine musk.

