## Candidate-survival and omission audit

The osmanthus accord has separate fruit-skin (Damascol/Damascenone/ionones), flesh (Jessemal/jasmones), floral light (Hedione/PEDMC/Freesia), suede (Suederal/Vetival), wood and skin states. Javanol is omitted: Ebanol owns creamy suede depth while Sandalore owns the fresh release, preventing a high-impact mineral-sandal takeover. No tobacco, rose pile, vanilla, lactone mass, or aggressive leather is present. Oranger/neroli are excluded to keep this distinct from LH-01. Quiet fixatives are not counted as audible complexity. **Damascol/Damascenone carrier-vector HOLD:** the intended 100 + 20 uL omission may proceed only after both actual stock carriers are verified, then replace each stock with its exact carrier volume. Substituting 120 uL DPG without that evidence is prohibited and the causal arm is HOLD.

### Modeled OAV < 1 survival dispositions

These dispositions are computational design decisions only; none labels an OAV-below-1 row as audible.

|#|Material|Modeled OAV|Disposition|Rationale class / precise role|Executable constant-total omission test|
|---:|---|---:|---|---|---|
|1|Cedarwood oil Virginia|0.424|KEEP_STRUCTURAL|SKIN_TEXTURE: low-headspace pencil grain dries the suede fold behind the osmanthus flesh|Replace 250 uL neat row with 250 uL DPG in a constant-total carrier-matched omission; compare suede dryness and wood monotony|
|2|Hexyl Salicylate|0.668|KEEP_STRUCTURAL|MATRIX: sheer low-headspace film carries floral flesh into the suede/sandal interior|Replace 300 uL neat row with 300 uL DPG in a constant-total carrier-matched omission; compare transition continuity and floral drag|
|3|Benzyl Benzoate|0.0014|KEEP_STRUCTURAL|FIXATION: disclosed quiet recurrence mass supports the fruit-shadow drydown without being counted as a smell facet|Replace 400 uL neat row with 400 uL DPG in a constant-total carrier-matched omission; compare persistence and compression|
|4|Tonka Bean Absolute|0.284|KEEP_STRUCTURAL|SKIN_TEXTURE: its labeled DPG stock supplies a low-headspace hay-grain underlay to the apricot suede|Replace 100 uL labeled stock with 100 uL DPG in a constant-total carrier-matched omission; compare dry fruit warmth and sweetness|
|5|Parmavert|0.961|KEEP_STRUCTURAL|SUBRECOGNITION: below-threshold green pressure keeps apricot flesh from becoming jammy or cosmetic|Replace 60 uL neat row with 60 uL DPG in a constant-total carrier-matched omission; compare peel/flesh definition and bitterness|
|6|Farnesol|0.166|KEEP_STRUCTURAL|FIXATION: low-headspace floral binder links osmanthus, Hedione, and the suede film without claiming an independent flower|Replace 20 uL neat row with 20 uL DPG in a constant-total carrier-matched omission; compare floral cohesion and blur|

## Inventory and stock audit

Live 2026-08-30 inventory governs. Osmanthus is the premium 10% DPG stock; volume-grade neat osmanthus is deliberately not silently substituted. Ambrettolide is the owned 10% DPG stock and the sole musk. Liquid Ambrofix, Bacdanol, Guaiacwood, depleted Polysantol and musks, Benzyl Salicylate, tinctures, and physics-incomplete Violet Leaf are absent from current. Givaudan AIMI physics is unresolved; the parser-visible current row uses canonical Alpha Isomethyl Ionone and no stock-specific OAV claim.

## Working-stock preparation ledger

`NOT AUTHORIZED.` Use existing Osmanthus 10% DPG, Beta Ionone 0.1% TEC, Tonka Absolute 10% DPG and Ambrettolide 10% DPG as labeled. Damascol 10%, Damascenone 1%, Suederal 10%, and Scentenal 1% are composition rows but their carrier identities remain unverified; no carrier-matched physical trial is executable until their labels or preparation records establish the actual carriers. Prepare Citral 10% from 100 uL + 900 uL DPG and Basil EO 10% from 100 uL + 900 uL DPG. Every source measurement and formula dose is at least 10 uL. Density, basis, homogeneity and stability uncertainties remain.

## Missing-chemical impact gate

Ginger CO2 is HIGH for literal warm rhizome; current jasmine tissue is only an approximation. Hedione HC is MEDIUM-HIGH for rear air; Hedione is not equivalent. Haitian Vetiver and Polysantol are MEDIUM for clean root and slow yield. Exact osmanthus lot composition is unknown, so the modeled natural OAV is partial authority and cannot prove apricot realism. Procure nothing before the present osmanthus/fruit-skin and suede modules survive controlled smelling.

## Future mixing order

`NO COMPOUNDING AUTHORIZED.` If later authorized: labeled stocks; quiet matrix; woods/sandal; suede/ionones; osmanthus/jasmine tissue; ginger/petitgrain aperture. Reconcile 6,000 uL before 24.00 mL ethanol. No safety/stability clearance follows.

## Controlled blinded test plan

V6 control versus LH-02 is a planned constant-6,000-uL comparison using two independently prepared complete sets, anonymous codes, AB/BA order, equal application, separated sessions, and free description before scoring. It is **physical HOLD** until the Damascol, Damascenone, Suederal, and Scentenal carrier vector can be exactly reconstructed in the control. Read 0, 5, 30, 120 minutes, 6 and 24 hours. Score family recognizability separately from overall liking, opening/transition/drydown pleasure, re-smell desire, apricot skin, osmanthus floral body, suede finesse, mineral wood, skin residue, dimensionality, texture, intensity, jam, candy, cosmetic iris, harsh leather, rose/tobacco drift, muddiness and fatigue. Pairwise preference does not prove the fruit-skin module; use its exact-carrier omission arm only if implicated. Null/discordant results remain HOLD.

